  "title": "Secretary of the Puerto Rico Department of Family, federal responders and volunteers transfer infant care products for distribution to families impacted by Hurricane Maria",
  "description": "Glorimar Andújar, the Secretary of the Puerto Rico Department of Family, federal responders and volunteers transfer Federal Emergency Management Agency supplied infant care products from San Juan, Puerto Rico, to Vieques for distribution to families in the community impacted by Hurricane Maria, Oct. 12, 2017.  Hundreds of pounds of essential infant care items including diapers, formula, wipes, bottles and blankets were delivered to Vieques, the island municipality off the southeast coast of Puerto Rico. U.S. Coast Guard video by Petty Officer 2nd Class Matthew S. Masaschi",
